3. What's Already Good
• Clean layering and explicit seams. Aplicacion_C_Liquidacion has no project reference to infrastructure; every collaborator has an interface (IOperacionesTomi, IOperacionesT24, IValidadorEjecucion, IAppLogger, IOperacionServicio) and OperacionServicio takes all of them by constructor (OperacionServicio.cs (../../CALYPSO/Calypso_Liquidacion/Aplicacion_C_Liquidacion/OperacionServicio.cs):28-38). Business rules (validation, XML) are separate from I/O, which is what makes the fixes below cheap.
• Container verified at start-up and per-tick scope. ServiceHost.cs (../../CALYPSO/Calypso_Liquidacion/Calypso_Liquidacion/ServiceHost.cs):97 calls _containerDI.Verify(), and each tick runs inside AsyncScopedLifestyle.BeginScope (:131) with a cloned Configuracion (:88), so the per-tick state (FechaSistema, EsDiaHabil) never leaks between ticks.
• No SQL built from text. Both repositories call stored procedures with typed parameters (OperacionesTomiDao.cs (../../CALYPSO/Calypso_Liquidacion/Infraestructura_C_Liquidacion/Repositorios/OperacionesTomiDao.cs):53-69); the T24 reads go through the shared view adapter with a single parameter. No injection surface.
• Required parameters are validated by the shared library. ObtenerParametrosSistemaAsync(string) treats every listed key as required and throws when missing or empty (Parametrizacion.cs:239-248, 275), so the dictionary lookups at OperacionServicio.cs:88-89 cannot raise KeyNotFoundException after a successful call.
• The write is atomic and auditable. usp_CLiquidacion_InsLiquidacionCompleto runs SET XACT_ABORT ON, a single transaction, writes the liquidation, the pair and the PROC status together, logs to Auditoria.ErrorLog and re-throws. Rejected messages are stored with their reason, so no instruction silently disappears from the interchange table.
• XML is built with `XmlDocument`/`CreateTextNode` (VariablesProcessor.cs (../../CALYPSO/Calypso_Liquidacion/Aplicacion_C_Liquidacion/Helpers/VariablesProcessor.cs):31-86), so values are escaped; no string concatenation of XML.
• Cancellation is honoured between requests (OperacionServicio.cs:122) and the host shuts down through the shared base with a cleanup token (ServiceHost.cs:144-185).
• Regexes are compiled once into a static dictionary with named groups, so adding a message type is data, not a new branch.
• Real unit-test project. MSTest + Moq, method-level parallelism, Arrange/Act/Assert layout, descriptive Spanish names; the seams above make the orchestration mockable.
• Hygiene: no Console/Debug output, no DateTime.Now, no hard-coded connection strings or credentials, build output git-ignored.
