Issue: the loop checks the token at :122, then the message is parsed with a regex and ValidaOperacion checks it again at :242. If the service is stopped in that window the OperationCanceledException is swallowed by catch (Exception) and converted into Fallo(ex.ToString()). ProcesarSolicitudAsync (:162-175) then persists it as operacion_valida = 0 with the exception text as the reason, and usp_CLiquidacion_InsLiquidacionCompleto flips the interchange row to PROC. A valid liquidation is permanently rejected and will not be retried. The window is milliseconds wide for a normal message, but it is wider for slow messages (CL-FR-3), it opens on every deployment/stop, and the consequence is a lost payment instruction. The second ThrowIfCancellationRequested adds nothing the loop does not already do.
Fix:
Code block (csharp)
// ValidaOperacion: do not throw on cancellation, and never translate it into a business result
catch (OperationCanceledException) { throw; }
catch (Exception ex) { ... }
 
// ProcesarSolicitudAsync: leave the request in RECV when cancelled
catch (OperationCanceledException) when (ct.IsCancellationRequested) { return; }
Benefit: a stop leaves unfinished requests untouched (still RECV) so the next start processes them; no business state is derived from shutdown. Suggested JIRA: CL-1 (Major)
