Issue: PersistirOperacionAsync returns void and swallows every failure. The only thing that moves a row out of the work list is the UPDATE ... SET estatus = 'PROC' at the end of the stored procedure, which rolls back with the insert. If the insert fails for a data reason (for example @nom_cliente VARCHAR(150) receiving a longer COMPANY_NAME, CAST(@fecha_sistema AS INT), or a reason text longer than the err_descripcion column, see CL-FR-5), the row stays RECV, is selected again 5-10 seconds later, is parsed, queried in T24 and rejected by the database again, and raises one alert row per tick for as long as it exists. There is no attempt counter, no quarantine status and no de-duplication of the alert. The catch inside ProcesarSolicitudAsync (:178-182) tries a second insert with ERROR: ..., which fails for the same reason. Because the shared SQL runner hides the database error (CL-FR-17), the log does not even say why.
